# Images: checked spec

An image is what the kernels load and what `seed/deus.image` is: the closure of one entry point as
`(def "hash" core)` lines sorted by hash, a `(type …)` or `(ability …)` line for each user type and
ability they use, and `(main "hash")` ([deus/image.deus](../../deus/image.deus)). This document states
what an image holds and that it depends only on the code (task 1ab6c044). The laws build images from a
map of objects, so they read no store. Written in the order of the process (D92).

## Extensions

| Term | URI |
| --- | --- |
| `api` | `org.dxos.deus.api@1.0` |
| `req` | `org.dxos.deus.req@1.0` |

## APIs

```mdl
api A-1: building images
  signatures:
  - Image.build : (Text -> {Throw Text | e} Option Sexp) -> Text -> {Throw Text | e} Text
  - Image.closure : (Text -> {Throw Text | e} Option Sexp) -> List Text -> {Throw Text | e} List (Text, Sexp)
  - Image.load : (Text -> {Throw Text | e} Option Sexp) -> List Text -> {Throw Text | e} Unit
```

## Requirements

```mdl
req R-1: an image holds every definition its entry point reaches, each once, sorted by hash, and no other
  by: Image.Spec.closureIsReachable | Image.Spec.closureIgnoresRootOrder
```

```mdl
req R-2: a reference to a definition the store does not have fails the build and names its hash
  by: Image.Spec.missingDefinitionFails
```

```mdl
req R-3: each user type and ability the definitions construct, match or perform gets one line with its IRI; builtin types and unused ones get none
  by: Image.Spec.nominalLines
```

```mdl
req R-4: the last line names the entry point, and the image ends with a new line
  by: Image.Spec.mainLineLast
```

## Laws

Each law is a test under `Image.Spec`; `deus ls Image.Spec.` lists them.
